1
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:36,000
The new James Bond...living on the edge.

2
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
The Living Daylights is a action, adventure,
thriller film directed by John Glen.

3
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:36,000
After a defecting Russian general reveals a plot to assassinate foreign spies, James Bond is assigned a secret mission to
dispatch the new head of the KGB to prevent an escalation of tensions between the Soviet Union and the West.

4
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
James Bond, played by Timothy Dalton.

5
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Kara Milovy, played by Maryam D'Abo.

6
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Brad Whitaker, played by Joe Don Baker.

7
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Kamran Shah, played by Art Malik.

8
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
General Leonid Pushkin, played by John Rhys-Davies.

9
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
General Georgi Koskov, played by Jeroen Krabbé.

10
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The Living Daylights is a 1987 spy film, the fifteenth entry in the James Bond series produced by Eon
Productions, and the first of two to star Timothy Dalton as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.

11
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The fourth film in the series to be directed by John Glen, the film's title is taken from Ian Fleming's short
story "The Living Daylights", the plot of which also forms the basis of the first act of the film.

12
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It was the last film to use the title of an Ian Fleming
story until the 2006 instalment Casino Royale.

13
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:36,000
It is also the first film to have Caroline Bliss as
Miss Moneypenny, replacing Lois Maxwell.

14
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The Living Daylights was produced by Albert R.

15
01:37:30,000 --> 01:37:36,000
Broccoli, his stepson Michael G.

16
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
Wilson, and co-produced by his daughter, Barbara Broccoli.

17
01:50:30,000 --> 01:50:36,000
It grossed $191.2 million worldwide and was followed by Licence to Kill in 1989.

18
01:57:00,000 --> 01:57:06,000
The film explores themes of prison, london,
england, assassination, airplane, escape.

19
02:03:30,000 --> 02:03:36,000
The tone is intense.
